== Memorials ==
[[File:Major Somnath Sharma statue at Param Yodha Sthal Delhi.jpg|250px|thumb|right|Major Somnath Sharma's statue at ''Param Yodha Sthal'', [[National War Memorial (India)|National War Memorial]], New Delhi]]
In 2009 [[Balidan Stambh]], the war memorial in [[Jammu]] paid tribute to nine Param Vir Chakra awardees who attained martyrdom in Jammu and Kashmir by inscribing their name on the pillars erected in semi circumference for the respective wars in which they participated. Their names are displayed near the eternal flame and as relief mural on the semi circumference wall.<ref>{{Cite web|title=A Monument of Sacrifice|url=https://www.dailyexcelsior.com/a-monument-of-sacrifice-2/|publisher=Daily Excelsior|access-date=29 December 2024}}</ref>

In September  2014 a memorial has been built in the memory of PVC recipients at Marina Park, [[Port Blair]], in [[Andaman and Nicobar Islands]]. It was inaugurated by the [[Lieutenant Governors of Andaman and Nicobar|Lieutenant Governor of Andaman and Nicobar]] Lieutenant General [[A. K. Singh|Ajay Kumar Singh]], in the presence of the Commander-in-Chief [[Andaman and Nicobar Command]], Vice Admiral [[Pradeep Kumar Chatterjee]].<ref name="Param Vir Chakra Memorial dedicated to the nation">{{Cite web |last=[[Press Trust of India]] |date=18 September 2014 |title=Param Vir Chakra Memorial dedicated to the nation |url=http://www.dnaindia.com/india/report-param-vir-chakra-memorial-dedicated-to-the-nation-2019753 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180109190915/http://www.dnaindia.com/india/report-param-vir-chakra-memorial-dedicated-to-the-nation-2019753 |archive-date=9 January 2018 |access-date=9 January 2018 |website=Daily News and Analysis |publisher=Diligent Media Corporation Limited}}</ref>

On 2 May 2017, at a ceremony conducted in the [[National Media Centre, New Delhi|National Media Center]], [[New Delhi]], [[Minister of Defence (India)|Minister of State for Defence]] [[Subhash Bhamre]] inaugurated a campaign to build a "wall of valour" in a thousand educational institutions across the country. The campaign was initiated by the two serving receipts of PVC, Subedar [[Yogendra Singh Yadav]] and Naib Subedar [[Sanjay Kumar (soldier)|Sanjay Kumar]]. The campaign was named "Vidya Veerta Abhiyan". The objective is to build a wall of {{convert|15|by|20|ft|m|round=0.5|order=flip}} at various educational campuses with the voluntary contributions from the students and the faculty of respective institutions. These walls are to portray all 21 recipients of the PVC along with relevant information.<ref name="A ‘wall of valour' for our bravehearts in campuses">{{Cite web |last=Anil Bhat |date=10 May 2017 |title=A 'wall of valour' for our bravehearts in campuses |url=http://www.asianage.com/india/all-india/100517/a-wall-of-valour-for-our-bravehearts-in-campuses.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180109181040/http://www.asianage.com/india/all-india/100517/a-wall-of-valour-for-our-bravehearts-in-campuses.html |archive-date=9 January 2018 |access-date=9 January 2018 |website=[[The Asian Age]]}}</ref>

In 2019 Bronze Busts of all 21 recipients are installed in the Param Yodha Sthal, which is a part of the [[National War Memorial (India)|National War Memorial]]. The site is adjacent to the main memorial and has informative plaques displaying the citations of the heroes.<ref>{{Cite web |title=PM Modi unveils National War Memorial: 10 things to know about it – National War Memorial to be dedicated to soldiers |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/politics-and-nation/pm-modi-unveils-national-war-memorial-10-things-to-know-about-it/param-vir-chakra-awardees/slideshow/68148225.cms |website=The Economic Times}}</ref>

On January 23, 2023 (birth anniversary of Subhash Chandra Bose), the Indian government named 21 large uncharted islands in the [[Andaman Islands]] after the 21 recipients of the Param Vir Chakra.

== In popular culture ==
The TV series ''[[Param Vir Chakra (TV series)|Param Vir Chakra]]'' (1990), which focuses on the lives of Param Vir Chakra winners, was directed by [[Chetan Anand (director)|Chetan Anand]]. The first episode of the series featured the first recipient of the award, Major [[Somnath Sharma]] of the [[Kumaon Regiment]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Madhu Jain |date=15 August 1990 |title=Mandi House Hardsells Kashmir in its Serial 'Gul Gulshan Gulfam' |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/magazine/society-and-the-arts/media/story/19900815-mandi-house-hardsells-kashmir-in-its-serial-gul-gulshan-gulfam-812914-1990-08-14 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140814124434/http://indiatoday.intoday.in/story/mandi-house-hardsells-kashmir-in-its-serial-gul-gulshan-gulfam/1/315475.html |archive-date=14 August 2014 |access-date=13 August 2014 |website=India Today |df=dmy-all}}</ref><ref name="Goldie commands respect even 10 years after death">{{Cite web |title=Goldie Commands Respect Even 10 years After Death |url=http://www.sunday-guardian.com/investigation/goldie-commands-respect-even-10-years-after-death |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160921103221/http://www.sunday-guardian.com/investigation/goldie-commands-respect-even-10-years-after-death |archive-date=21 September 2016 |access-date=5 September 2016 |website=Sunday Guardian}}</ref><ref name="Maker of innovative, meaningful movies">{{Cite web |date=15 June 2007 |title=Maker of Innovative, Meaningful Movies |url=http://www.thehindu.com/todays-paper/tp-features/tp-fridayreview/maker-of-innovative-meaningful-movies/article2272748.ece |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180228184000/http://www.thehindu.com/todays-paper/tp-features/tp-fridayreview/maker-of-innovative-meaningful-movies/article2272748.ece |archive-date=28 February 2018 |access-date=5 September 2016 |website=The Hindu |language=en-IN}}</ref>

Indian [[Punjabi language|Punjabi]]-language biopic movie ''[[Subedar Joginder Singh (film)|Subedar Joginder Singh]]'' (2018) is based on [[Joginder Singh (soldier)|Singh's]] life and his action during Sino-Indian War.<ref>{{Citation |title=Subedar Joginder Singh Review {2.5/5}: If movies served with a generous dose of national pride are your scene, then this one should not be missed |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/movie-reviews/subedar-joginder-singh/movie-review/63652256.cms |work=The Times of India |access-date=28 November 2021}}</ref>

A [[graphic novel]] titled ''Param Vir Chakra by Amar Chitra Katha'', a comic book released in 2015 featuring 21 dedicated and concise stories.
<ref>{{cite book|last=Puri|first=Reena|title=Param Vir Chakra|url=https://us.amarchitrakatha.com/products/param-vir-chakra?srsltid=AfmBOoqWTSyUiI7Eg2DFYy6uviDWA_GL1zCjrXvBMIo1-wpCmS6UZKg7|publisher=Amar Chitra Katha|pages=229–243|isbn=9789350858424|access-date=20 December 2024}}</ref>

